{
  "id": "phase-088",
  "title": "Make the reachability-only tests assert the value they reach for",
  "severity": "major",
  "depends_on": [],
  "risk": "low",
  "finding": "Three groups of tests prove a code path RUNS and cannot prove it runs correctly. tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs:232-237 walks six builtins (`abs`, `uppercase`, `trim`, `sqrt`, `text.uppercase`, `text.split`) through the bytecode VM with `Ok(_) => {}` and a `panic!` only on `Err` - so `sqrt` returning 1 instead of 1.4142135623730951, or `split` returning one element instead of two, both pass. tests/loop_bounds_test.rs:586-591 runs `repeat \"five\" times` with `say \"never\"` in the body and asserts only that the run succeeded; `vm.take_output()` is never called, so the test passes whether or not the loop body ran at all. tests/loop_bounds_test.rs:596-601 is the identical shape for `for each x in 5`. tests/redblue_test.rs is five tests that each call `run_source` and assert `result.is_ok()`, and src/lib.rs:105 discards the value with `result.map(|_| ())`, so no test in that file can detect a wrong answer. Twenty tests across tests/ have no reachable `assert!` or `assert_eq!` at all for the same reason. The suite reports 1,414 passing, which is exactly what makes the gap invisible.",
  "goal": "Make every test that claims output was or was not produced actually read the output, so a builtin that answers the wrong value fails the suite.",
  "must_touch": [
    "tests/"
  ],
  "accept": [
    "tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs:232 asserts the bytecode VM's VALUE for all six builtins rather than `Ok(_)`; every expected value is written literally in the test, not derived from the implementation",
    "tests/loop_bounds_test.rs:586 and :596 call `take_output()` and assert it is empty - the literal `never` inside each loop body is what makes that assertion possible",
    "each of the five tests in tests/redblue_test.rs asserts the exact output its program produces",
    "the twenty tests with no reachable `assert!` or `assert_eq!` are each either given one or deleted, and REPORT.md lists every one with its reason - a deleted test is replaced by one that can fail, never silently dropped",
    "the `cargo test` total is NOT lower than the 1,414 measured at audit time, which is the machine-checkable form of 'nothing was deleted to make the suite quieter'",
    "edge_* tests cover: a builtin returning the wrong value on each engine, a loop body that must not run, a program whose correct output is the empty string, and a program whose output is non-empty",
    "`cargo test` reports 0 failures and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean"
  ],
  "timeout_min": 120
